                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "18743282",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198089268976",
                            "num_reviews": 2,
                            "playtime_forever": 54,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 54,
                            "last_played": 1445964031
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I really don't want to give any game a negative review but since Devoured Time isn't a game yet I have no problems this time. I bought the game, started it up, and found tabs for a handful of different game modes. Alas, only the tutorial and the main game tabs seemed accessable so I chose the tutorial. Once in I was unable to interact with anything at all, thus rendering the tutorial a waste of time. Okay, that's fine, it's EA of course, so I tried the main game. That turned out to be the exact same thing as the tutorial. The only other playing options were 2 tabs that were for testing- TESTING!! \n\nI decided to withold any negative thoughts and instead posted my problem on the forums, thinking maybe I had missed something. The next day one of the Devs (beast) replied to my post stating I shouldn't have been able to access the main menu tab in the first place because he is still working on it to get it ready. Oh really? Then why is this product ( I refuse to call it a game anymore) on here? I can't say for sure but with such decietfully misleading info being given to entice the unwary to purchase this product, I don't have much faith in the people involved as of now. I may be shown to be wrong and hope I end up wrong. If that happens I will personally apoligise to Beast and will update this review to reflect any positive changes taking this product foreward but for now stay away from it. Star far away!",
